WEBVTT

00:06.630 --> 00:10.160
Seven people bought the book that I made.

00:12.140 --> 00:14.660
I didn't know what to expect in the beginning,

00:15.210 --> 00:17.680
but in the end, I'm glad I participated.

00:18.140 --> 00:19.410
Taishi?

00:22.280 --> 00:23.510
What's the matter?

00:26.690 --> 00:28.550
This is sudden, but...

00:28.550 --> 00:29.450
Huh?

00:29.450 --> 00:30.460
We have none.

00:30.460 --> 00:31.290
Of what?

00:31.490 --> 00:32.290
Money.

00:32.590 --> 00:33.750
M-money?

00:34.060 --> 00:38.430
Precisely! Money! Dough! Cash!

00:39.200 --> 00:41.220
The fee for printing and producing the book!

00:41.700 --> 00:42.900
Registration fee for the booth!

00:42.900 --> 00:45.060
This and that! Those and these!

00:45.470 --> 00:49.840
Using differentiation and integration on everything...

00:49.840 --> 00:53.410
...from various angles has led to this piece of detail!

00:51.410 --> 00:54.540
In The Red

00:55.050 --> 00:57.210
That's a pretty simple conclusion.

00:57.980 --> 01:01.820
Red! A burning red!

01:01.820 --> 01:05.190
Red! That is my soul!

01:03.460 --> 01:06.950
Wait, then what about the printing fees for Chisa?

01:07.330 --> 01:10.090
I'm having her wait for it!

01:11.860 --> 01:14.390
Whoa, you mean...

01:15.170 --> 01:16.630
We're in debt?!

01:16.630 --> 01:18.430
Oh, yeah!

01:21.440 --> 01:25.000
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

01:25.540 --> 01:28.680
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

01:28.680 --> 01:32.240
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

01:32.450 --> 01:35.510
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

01:35.790 --> 01:39.390
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

01:39.390 --> 01:42.960
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

01:42.960 --> 01:46.330
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

01:46.530 --> 01:50.060
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

01:50.140 --> 01:53.540
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

01:53.740 --> 01:57.140
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

01:57.310 --> 02:01.710
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

02:01.910 --> 02:04.850
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

02:05.150 --> 02:11.060
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

02:11.420 --> 02:18.130
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

02:18.800 --> 02:22.800
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

02:22.800 --> 02:25.970
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

02:25.970 --> 02:29.710
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

02:29.710 --> 02:32.970
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

02:33.040 --> 02:36.810
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

02:37.180 --> 02:40.290
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

02:40.290 --> 02:43.880
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

02:44.090 --> 02:46.990
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

02:49.990 --> 02:56.800
WE REALLY HAVE

02:49.990 --> 02:56.800
NO MONEY!

03:13.820 --> 03:17.020
Let's see, I'm pretty sure it's around here somewhere.

03:18.890 --> 03:21.050
PART-

03:18.890 --> 03:21.050
TIME

03:18.890 --> 03:21.050
JOB,

03:18.890 --> 03:21.050
COSMIX

03:18.890 --> 03:21.050
THIS IS

03:18.890 --> 03:21.050
THE PLACE,

03:18.890 --> 03:21.050
BROTHER!

03:18.890 --> 03:21.050
YAMAGIWA

03:22.930 --> 03:24.330
Good grief.

03:25.630 --> 03:29.830
Thus, you have no choice but to aim to expand our working capital!

03:30.370 --> 03:33.370
But our group name is "Brother 2", after all,

03:33.370 --> 03:35.140
so you should bear part of the burden of debt, too...

03:35.570 --> 03:37.510
Non, non, Comrade Kazuki.

03:37.910 --> 03:39.400
Creating doujinshi.

03:39.910 --> 03:40.970
Selling it.

03:41.150 --> 03:42.840
Earning funds for the next one.

03:43.210 --> 03:48.080
Experiencing this beautiful cycle is part of your education, comrade.

03:48.650 --> 03:50.210
And so!

03:50.860 --> 03:52.550
Part-time job!

03:53.190 --> 03:55.850
Work hard with sweat upon your brow, my brother!

03:56.130 --> 03:57.860
For our next ambition!

04:00.970 --> 04:01.800
But...

04:01.330 --> 04:04.130
"Yamagiwa"

04:02.070 --> 04:04.130
I thought this was the town of electronics, but...

04:05.170 --> 04:07.440
"Rocks Roat

04:05.170 --> 04:07.440
Game Software 6F"

04:05.170 --> 04:08.270
"Animania"

04:05.800 --> 04:07.270
It's sort of...

04:06.770 --> 04:08.270
"Game Palace"

04:08.940 --> 04:10.910
I don't know how you got the legendary doujinshi.

04:10.910 --> 04:12.940
What do you want to do about lunch?

04:12.080 --> 04:13.600
You wanna go to Oden Hall?

04:19.620 --> 04:21.090
It's around here.

04:22.490 --> 04:23.980
Here's a coupon!

04:25.520 --> 04:27.220
Oh, no photographs, please.

04:28.230 --> 04:29.760
Here you go, a coupon.

04:29.230 --> 04:30.660
No, I'm...

04:30.400 --> 04:32.030
Cosplay cafe, CosMlX!

04:32.030 --> 04:35.360
Today's costumes are from the hugely popular Steel Angel Kurumi!

04:35.670 --> 04:37.230
D-don't tell me...

04:39.200 --> 04:40.730
The cafe is upstairs.

04:40.940 --> 04:41.740
WELCOME

04:51.980 --> 04:54.650
"Anime Shop Paro"

04:52.180 --> 04:54.650
You're kidding me, right?!

04:55.720 --> 04:57.990
It's not a joke, Master!

04:58.190 --> 05:00.020
All drinks are 20% off.

05:00.360 --> 05:02.450
The coupon's a very good deal.

05:02.690 --> 05:04.720
No, I'm not here for that...

05:08.130 --> 05:10.190
Hi, there! You okay?

05:22.050 --> 05:23.380
Reiko, you're late!

05:23.380 --> 05:25.150
Did you go and pass out the coupons?

05:25.280 --> 05:26.770
You can count on me!

05:27.250 --> 05:29.380
These are all customers?

05:32.190 --> 05:33.920
Operation complete!

05:34.060 --> 05:36.960
All these people are my spoils for the day!

05:37.900 --> 05:39.560
Reiko, you're so in character!

05:39.560 --> 05:42.120
Truly the guardian of justice, Lord Gasshu!

05:51.010 --> 05:54.110
Oh, you're the new part-timer, aren't you?!

05:53.850 --> 05:54.680
Uh-oh.

05:54.280 --> 05:56.010
What? Oh, really?

05:56.010 --> 05:57.980
Then, come on over here.

05:57.980 --> 06:01.540
No, I'm... I'm...

06:06.920 --> 06:08.950
Nice. You've got the right look.

06:09.130 --> 06:10.990
I'm telling you, I'm...that is...

06:11.930 --> 06:14.130
He's right! Do you cosplay a lot?

06:14.130 --> 06:16.570
No, I've never done this before.

06:17.140 --> 06:21.070
Well, Kuhonbutsu introduced you to us, so let's not mind the details.

06:21.070 --> 06:24.240
We'll take you on for two weeks as an emergency fill-in.

06:24.410 --> 06:26.410
Oh, but I'm...well...

06:26.410 --> 06:29.750
Oh, sorry, sorry, we haven't introduced ourselves yet.

06:30.110 --> 06:31.670
I'm Reiko Haga.

06:31.820 --> 06:34.910
And those three over there are Miho, Mayu, and Yuka.

06:35.620 --> 06:37.490
We look forward to working with you, starting tomorrow.

06:37.490 --> 06:39.480
Uh, s-sure...

06:43.490 --> 06:45.830
What's the big idea, Taishi?!

06:46.400 --> 06:49.860
You didn't say anything about it being that kind of place!

06:50.170 --> 06:50.970
Hey!

06:51.140 --> 06:52.360
Fool!

06:52.600 --> 06:53.260
What?

06:53.570 --> 06:56.070
Two birds with one stone!
One order of take out!

06:56.070 --> 06:58.700
It is all for the sake of the never-ending future!

06:59.240 --> 07:02.180
Never mind the jokes.
I don't want to talk about the future.

07:02.180 --> 07:04.480
I'm worried about today!

07:04.480 --> 07:05.550
This summer...

07:05.550 --> 07:06.210
Huh?

07:06.680 --> 07:09.680
A miraculous festival that never existed before will be born.

07:13.190 --> 07:16.160
It rivals the beginning of the universe, the Big Bang,

07:17.730 --> 07:23.530
the birth of everything, even the creation of the world...

07:30.210 --> 07:33.340
And this summer, the place of decisive battle we will head for...

07:33.340 --> 07:36.870
Atop Chomo-Lungma-- No you could even liken it to Mount Olympus...

07:37.120 --> 07:39.580
The place closest to the gods...

07:39.880 --> 07:40.720
That is...

07:41.720 --> 07:42.450
That is...?

07:48.030 --> 07:49.430
This!

07:49.660 --> 07:52.320
Comic Party?

07:53.060 --> 07:56.660
Well, to put it simply, a very large exhibition and spot sale.

07:57.300 --> 08:00.270
You couldn't even begin comparin' it to the other ones.

08:01.340 --> 08:03.740
Indeed! Multiple exhibition and spot sales...

08:03.740 --> 08:06.230
...fused together like a thermo-nuclear reaction!

08:06.610 --> 08:10.050
A super-ultra-mega-giant-big exhibition and spot sale...

08:10.050 --> 08:11.980
...of a scale never seen before!

08:12.550 --> 08:16.750
So? How's that party thing related to the part-time job?

08:16.750 --> 08:19.850
It's like this, Kazuki.

08:20.660 --> 08:22.330
You're acting weird, Taishi.

08:22.330 --> 08:25.630
We're in debt, and if we don't earn the printing fees now,

08:25.630 --> 08:29.260
we won't be able to put out a new issue at Comic Party, Comi-Pa for short.

08:29.500 --> 08:32.330
Then, I could go work at a different place...

08:35.410 --> 08:37.410
The spirit of Shiatsu is the spirit of a parent!

08:37.410 --> 08:40.310
Can you not understand how I feel, Comrade?!

08:41.010 --> 08:41.650
Huh?

08:41.650 --> 08:44.650
That cafe is the trendy spot of the doujin world!

08:44.650 --> 08:47.050
It is my parental sentiment that you will study there in person...

08:47.050 --> 08:50.290
and that there is something for you to gain there.

08:50.290 --> 08:51.810
Do you understand?!

08:52.290 --> 08:54.350
But studying...

08:54.560 --> 08:56.590
Yes, study.

08:56.590 --> 08:57.320
Uh-oh.

08:58.160 --> 09:00.430
The bell rang and class started long ago.

09:00.430 --> 09:02.170
Are you finished, Sendou?

09:02.170 --> 09:04.760
Y-yes, pardon me.

09:09.810 --> 09:10.780
Are you listening to me?!

09:10.780 --> 09:12.110
Y-yes, Sir!

09:13.440 --> 09:14.210
Idiot...

09:16.050 --> 09:17.540
But...a part-time job?

09:18.150 --> 09:20.620
"Anime Shop Paro"

09:27.160 --> 09:31.600
Let's see, table #5 hasn't ordered yet, and table #8 is...

09:31.760 --> 09:33.460
I'd like to order, please.

09:33.460 --> 09:34.830
Oh, right away!

09:35.130 --> 09:36.330
Can we have water, already?

09:37.000 --> 09:38.240
Oh, yes Sir!

09:38.240 --> 09:39.330
I'd like another coffee.

09:39.400 --> 09:41.240
Yes Sir, I'll bring it right away!

09:46.210 --> 09:48.240
Daisy, where's our menus?

09:48.480 --> 09:49.710
Right here!

09:49.710 --> 09:51.340
Lily, we'd like to order!

09:52.020 --> 09:53.450
I understand, Sir.

09:53.750 --> 09:55.220
I want a hot milk.

09:55.220 --> 09:55.790
Me, too.

09:55.790 --> 09:58.780
All right, cheers with milk.

10:01.090 --> 10:02.630
Momopi!

10:02.630 --> 10:04.930
Do the Lovely Operation Tempete!

10:04.930 --> 10:07.090
Cleanse me, too!

10:09.330 --> 10:11.130
Everyone's so into it.

10:16.570 --> 10:20.240
Sheesh, everything's so jumbled, I can't tell what's what.

10:23.180 --> 10:24.980
It should be around here.

10:30.790 --> 10:33.780
"Anime Shop Paro"

10:36.930 --> 10:37.900
No way...

10:57.580 --> 10:59.980
Please come in, the cafe is this way!

11:01.720 --> 11:03.020
Welcome!

11:03.020 --> 11:05.120
The entrance to CosMlX is here, right?

11:05.120 --> 11:05.890
Yes!

11:05.890 --> 11:07.450
Come on, let's go in.

11:12.560 --> 11:14.960
Hi, you getting used to it yet?

11:16.500 --> 11:18.230
Everyone's so intense...

11:19.600 --> 11:22.070
Oh, this? It's a new character making its debut today!

11:22.070 --> 11:24.910
It's a popular character from the hugely popular game,

11:24.910 --> 11:26.310
Supreme Fight King!

11:26.310 --> 11:30.270
A girl with the 4000 year mystique of China, Chaichai.

11:31.120 --> 11:33.280
I-I see...that's amazing.

11:33.420 --> 11:36.180
Reiko, please take this to table #4.

11:36.650 --> 11:37.590
Okay!

11:37.860 --> 11:40.350
Sendou, go back to work soon too, okay?

11:40.930 --> 11:41.690
Yes, Sir.

11:44.560 --> 11:46.000
Thank you for waiting.

11:47.970 --> 11:50.600
I knew there was a hobby called cosplaying...

11:50.600 --> 11:52.540
...and I saw it at
Odaiba in the spring, but...

11:59.210 --> 12:02.370
I still don't quite get it.

12:06.680 --> 12:07.910
Welco...

12:11.420 --> 12:13.410
W-why is Mizuki here?

12:23.400 --> 12:24.800
Welcome!

12:26.100 --> 12:27.200
U-um...

12:27.670 --> 12:30.070
Would that seat over there be all right with you?

12:30.070 --> 12:31.100
Y-yes.

12:32.780 --> 12:34.940
I'll bring you a glass of water in just a second.

12:35.710 --> 12:38.950
Sendou, please go take the order from table #12.

12:38.950 --> 12:39.640
Wha?!

12:40.150 --> 12:41.380
What's the matter?

12:41.490 --> 12:43.320
No, well, um...

12:47.530 --> 12:48.820
I understand.

12:52.430 --> 12:53.730
What would you like?

12:54.170 --> 12:56.430
H-h-h-here is your m-menu.

12:56.600 --> 13:00.330
I'll come back again when you've decided what to order.

13:00.910 --> 13:01.840
Kazuki.

13:02.770 --> 13:06.610
Wh-who is that? I am from the angel world...

13:06.610 --> 13:08.010
You seem to be having fun.

13:08.280 --> 13:10.810
No, there's a reason for this.

13:11.320 --> 13:12.870
The reason doesn't matter!

13:13.250 --> 13:15.990
I made Taishi talk, and found out where you're working!

13:15.990 --> 13:17.850
Kazuki, what's happened to you?!

13:18.690 --> 13:20.620
Before I knew it, you were completely into it!

13:20.620 --> 13:22.530
And now, you even dress weird like that!

13:22.530 --> 13:24.890
No, this is from Wedding Peach...

13:25.030 --> 13:28.190
Weddings and bridal stuff have nothing to do with this!

13:28.300 --> 13:29.290
Is she your friend?

13:29.470 --> 13:30.330
Oh, yeah.

13:30.330 --> 13:32.600
Friend? Why, of course!

13:32.600 --> 13:34.110
We've only been in the same class...

13:34.110 --> 13:36.270
...and only known each other since middle school!

13:36.270 --> 13:38.300
Just friends!

13:38.840 --> 13:39.910
Besides...

13:39.910 --> 13:42.510
Just a picture should be no problem!

13:43.710 --> 13:45.050
It is only natural to render such service...

13:45.050 --> 13:46.750
...at an establishment made to entertain guests.

13:46.750 --> 13:49.050
I'll take pretty pictures.

13:53.860 --> 13:54.850
Yeah.

13:58.830 --> 14:01.270
This cafe doesn't allow photographs, right?

14:01.270 --> 14:03.530
Yeah, it's posted on the door, too.

14:03.970 --> 14:05.460
Never mind that!

14:07.070 --> 14:08.440
Sorry, give me a second.

14:12.410 --> 14:14.170
Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

14:22.450 --> 14:23.980
You look very nice.

14:24.860 --> 14:27.690
My camera skills have already been proven,

14:27.690 --> 14:30.720
seeing how I'm secretly a regular subscriber of photography magazines.

14:30.800 --> 14:34.530
What? Really?
I'm going to be in a magazine?

14:34.530 --> 14:37.300
Well, that depends on you, the model, of course.

14:37.940 --> 14:41.870
No way! Then I think I'll make a special exception for you!

14:42.440 --> 14:46.540
Be in character and pose.

14:46.710 --> 14:47.610
Like this?

14:47.610 --> 14:49.100
That's good, that's good!

14:51.550 --> 14:52.820
Excuse me...

14:52.520 --> 14:54.720
Don't let them take anymore, Miho!

14:55.050 --> 14:58.720
Oh, Reiko, look, look.
I'm going to be in a magazine!

14:58.920 --> 15:02.190
You're wrong. It's probably some kind of pervy magazine...

15:02.190 --> 15:04.790
...that takes submissions or something.

15:05.800 --> 15:07.160
But a little won't hurt.

15:07.160 --> 15:08.150
No, you shouldn't!

15:08.630 --> 15:11.770
If you're going to go so far, then we shall photograph you, too.

15:11.770 --> 15:13.140
That's right.

15:13.140 --> 15:16.510
You're just mad that you're not being photographed, anyway.

15:16.940 --> 15:18.000
You're wrong!

15:19.040 --> 15:21.710
These costumes show our love for the characters!

15:22.010 --> 15:24.750
This cafe is for people who sincerely enjoy cosplaying.

15:24.750 --> 15:28.210
It's not a place to take weird pictures and defile the characters!

15:28.620 --> 15:30.920
This is our form of love!

15:30.920 --> 15:31.790
Yeah, yeah!

15:31.790 --> 15:32.780
Sirs!

15:33.690 --> 15:35.180
Here is more water for you.

15:35.930 --> 15:37.060
We didn't ask for...

15:37.060 --> 15:37.820
And...

15:38.160 --> 15:39.890
Photos are not allowed at this establishment!

15:46.300 --> 15:47.570
Here's your money!

15:47.570 --> 15:49.470
What an unpleasant cafe!

15:50.740 --> 15:51.900
Sirs!

15:53.940 --> 15:55.810
You're 200 yen short...

15:59.580 --> 16:00.720
Off we go!

16:00.720 --> 16:03.290
Yeah, yeah!

16:01.390 --> 16:03.290
Run, run!

16:09.630 --> 16:12.120
I'm sorry, Reiko.
I got carried away.

16:13.160 --> 16:16.530
Don't sweat it.
I can understand how you felt, too.

16:16.530 --> 16:18.170
That was nerve-wracking.

16:18.170 --> 16:20.070
By the way, what about your friend?

16:29.050 --> 16:29.950
Mizuki...

16:52.770 --> 16:54.400
Well, I'll be leaving now.

16:55.170 --> 16:56.610
I'll see you tomorrow.

16:56.610 --> 16:58.670
Yes, thank you very much.

17:12.820 --> 17:15.090
I bet Mizuki's mad.

17:18.000 --> 17:19.550
Hi, there!

17:23.870 --> 17:24.990
Miss Reiko!

17:25.540 --> 17:26.970
You scared me.

17:28.140 --> 17:31.910
Sorry about that. You looked kind of sad from behind, so...

17:32.240 --> 17:33.010
Re-really?

17:35.180 --> 17:36.770
What is it?

17:37.350 --> 17:40.080
Cosplay is love, huh?

17:42.390 --> 17:46.360
I guess I did say something like that, didn't I? How embarrassing.

17:46.360 --> 17:47.890
But when I heard you say that,

17:47.890 --> 17:50.590
I felt like I understood cosplaying a bit better.

17:51.000 --> 17:57.270
Until just a while ago, I used to think doujinshi was a weird hobby,

17:58.000 --> 17:58.870
but I don't know.

17:58.870 --> 18:00.400
The people who make them and buy them...

18:00.400 --> 18:02.430
...both have a certain love for it.

18:02.740 --> 18:08.870
Like love for books, love for comics, and love for anime.

18:09.180 --> 18:11.840
I thought it must be the same for cosplaying.

18:12.450 --> 18:13.350
Station!

18:13.580 --> 18:14.280
What?

18:14.490 --> 18:16.690
Sendou, you take the train, right?

18:16.690 --> 18:17.490
Yeah.

18:17.490 --> 18:19.750
Shall we go home together, part of the way?

18:23.760 --> 18:25.790
You probably don't know it, Sendou,

18:26.060 --> 18:28.570
but just recently, really gaudy cosplays...

18:28.570 --> 18:30.760
...and bad-mannered came-ko were on the rise.

18:31.300 --> 18:32.170
Cameko?

18:33.800 --> 18:35.170
It's short for camera boys.

18:36.210 --> 18:37.800
Meaning, people like today...

18:38.910 --> 18:40.980
It got to the point where cosplaying was banned...

18:40.980 --> 18:43.310
...from some exhibition and spot sales.

18:43.950 --> 18:46.180
I was only cosplaying because
I liked the game characters...

18:46.180 --> 18:48.820
...and I wanted to be like them.

18:48.820 --> 18:52.260
There are only a handful of those extreme people...

18:53.860 --> 18:55.860
I envy people like you, Sendou.

18:55.860 --> 18:57.330
What? Me?

18:57.660 --> 18:59.560
Because you can draw, right?

18:59.900 --> 19:01.830
I just started, though.

19:02.000 --> 19:03.970
I can't draw,

19:03.970 --> 19:07.930
so I can only express my love of the characters through cosplaying.

19:08.940 --> 19:11.970
But that's just another form of love.

19:16.110 --> 19:17.810
Sorry, was that too cheesy?

19:18.220 --> 19:19.110
Yeah, very.

19:20.450 --> 19:23.690
But you know, the big event coming up this summer...

19:23.690 --> 19:25.390
...isn't just going to be an exhibition and spot sale.

19:25.390 --> 19:27.490
They're going to have cosplay contests, too,

19:27.490 --> 19:29.590
so we're all looking forward to it.

19:29.890 --> 19:31.260
Is that Comi-Pa?

19:31.260 --> 19:34.030
Oh, you know it, too!

19:34.430 --> 19:38.270
You could say that.
I'm working to earn funds for it.

19:38.270 --> 19:41.470
I see! So, you're also going to be participating in Comi-Pa!

19:54.450 --> 19:57.920
<i>Shinjuku. Shinjuku.</i>

19:55.250 --> 19:56.950
Oh, I have to switch trains here.

20:00.120 --> 20:02.030
Well, I'll see you tomorrow.

20:02.330 --> 20:03.850
Yeah, later.

20:05.460 --> 20:07.860
Make sure you patch things up with your girlfriend.

20:08.170 --> 20:08.890
What?

20:13.070 --> 20:14.300
Girlfriend...?

20:17.940 --> 20:18.780
I'm home.

20:18.780 --> 20:21.680
Welcome back. There's a letter for you.

20:21.980 --> 20:22.970
A letter?

20:23.750 --> 20:26.720
"To Mr. Kazuki Sendou"

20:40.230 --> 20:42.260
Awesome! This is awesome!

20:43.700 --> 20:45.440
"There were various aspects of your book...

20:45.440 --> 20:46.990
"...that were crude in terms of technique,

20:47.870 --> 20:51.500
"but I was struck by the overflowing enthusiasm packed into those pages.

20:51.640 --> 20:54.610
"Keep it up, and good luck on your new issue for the summer."

20:55.580 --> 20:57.910
Miss Ikumi Tachikawa, huh?

20:58.150 --> 21:00.520
It's a fan letter. Addressed to me!

21:01.390 --> 21:03.880
"Good luck on your new issue for the summer," huh?

21:04.320 --> 21:06.050
All right, I'm going to do it!

21:06.460 --> 21:07.690
I'm not Reiko,

21:07.690 --> 21:11.150
but I've gotta finish up a great work that only I can make!

21:11.500 --> 21:13.590
Onward to Comic Party!

21:14.930 --> 21:16.730
Yes, yes, yes.

21:19.340 --> 21:20.030
Mizuki?

21:21.610 --> 21:23.540
He-hello?

21:27.510 --> 21:30.500
Sorry about leaving you alone at the cafe...

21:31.580 --> 21:33.550
Y-you know...

21:33.950 --> 21:34.650
Huh?

21:35.350 --> 21:37.010
<i>You were dressed weird, but...</i>

21:37.920 --> 21:40.450
<i>You looked just a little cool.</i>

21:40.760 --> 21:41.450
Huh?

21:41.990 --> 21:42.860
That's all!

22:20.330 --> 22:24.570
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:24.570 --> 22:29.030
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:29.170 --> 22:33.580
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:33.740 --> 22:37.650
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:37.650 --> 22:41.750
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:41.750 --> 22:46.020
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:46.190 --> 22:50.630
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:50.760 --> 22:54.800
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:54.800 --> 22:58.340
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:58.340 --> 23:03.270
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:03.410 --> 23:06.910
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:06.910 --> 23:12.350
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:13.420 --> 23:17.850
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:17.850 --> 23:21.890
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:21.890 --> 23:26.430
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:26.430 --> 23:35.400
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>

23:55.990 --> 24:20.280
PREVIEW

23:59.560 --> 24:01.700
What do you think of this new costume, Sendou?

24:01.700 --> 24:03.770
Wow, Reiko, I can't believe you're dressed like that!

24:03.770 --> 24:06.270
Look, look, this is how it is over here.

24:06.740 --> 24:08.470
And it's like this over here.

24:08.970 --> 24:10.910
I can do poses like this, too!

24:11.780 --> 24:13.310
What's the matter?

24:13.780 --> 24:17.650
Well, it is unfortunate that we cannot show this to our audience.

24:17.650 --> 24:19.450
Next time, "That's The Problem."

24:19.450 --> 24:21.450
Hey, that's my line!

24:20.880 --> 24:26.350
NEXT TIME

24:20.880 --> 24:26.350
THAT'S

24:20.880 --> 24:26.350
THE

24:20.880 --> 24:26.350
PROBLEM

24:21.450 --> 24:23.050
Fan service, fan service!
